; ============================================================================
; BSYS_CrossUDE
; ============================================================================
; xNVSE OnActivate on VFortBennyCrucifiedRef by the player - the same event
; BHYSYS hands the safe key over on. Crucified, Benny only dies if the
; player kills him, so the ledger changes hands here instead, before the
; vanilla script starts his dialogue. Alive check: once he's dead that key
; is the loot menu, and the body path has served him. BookSpawnUDF with
; PlayerREF hands over the book and his cut of the caps once - a later
; kill owes nothing.
; ============================================================================

Create: BSYS_CrossUDE

ref rActivated
ref rActionRef
ref rMe

Begin Function { rActivated, rActionRef }
  if VFortBennyCrucifiedRef.GetDead
    return
  endif

  ; A mid-save install after he's already on the cross never started a
  ; spree - nothing to hand over
  if Player.AuxVarGetFlt "_BSYS_iEnded" == 0
    return
  endif

  ; PlayerREF as the "corpse" = hand-over mode
  let rMe := PlayerREF
  Call BSYS_BookSpawnUDF rMe
End
